%% Novara — typical authenticated API request
%% See docs/Engineering-Bible/04-API.md, 08-Authentication.md
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User (browser)
    participant FE as project-novara (React)
    participant Clerk as Clerk
    participant BE as api-server (Express)
    participant MW as requireAuth middleware
    participant DB as Neon Postgres

    U->>FE: interacts with a page (e.g. Dashboard)
    FE->>Clerk: getToken() (Clerk React SDK)
    Clerk-->>FE: session JWT
    FE->>BE: fetch /api/contacts<br/>Authorization: Bearer <token>
    BE->>BE: clerkMiddleware verifies token,<br/>attaches auth state to req
    BE->>MW: requireAuth(req, res, next)
    alt no valid session
        MW-->>FE: 401 { error: "Unauthorized" }
    else valid session
        MW->>BE: req.userId = verified Clerk userId
        BE->>DB: SELECT * FROM contacts<br/>WHERE user_id = $1<br/>ORDER BY next_follow_up_date ASC
        DB-->>BE: rows
        BE->>BE: dbToContact() row -> camelCase
        BE-->>FE: 200 [...contacts]
        FE->>FE: TanStack Query caches result<br/>(staleTime: 30s)
        FE-->>U: renders contact list
    end
